        "created_at": "2015-05-01T13:53:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"silopolis\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silopolis/48/2166_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> silopolis:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>More time and effort has been spent explaining why you chose to go with the initials/acronyms than would have been spent making them a little more viewer-friendly in the first place.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not from my perspective. I pop in, amuse myself by watching everyone flog a dead horse, then post to ensure that they realize they weren't talking about what I really said, but about what their hive mind has agreed that I said. I'm just forcing them to go back to the beginning, because they start accusing me of things I never did. They communally agree that I did it, so I must have.</p>\n<p>I find threads like these highly amusing. I really am just laughing at everyone posting about this. They have missed something, because they have unreasonable expectations and feel they do not need to pay any attention. I just wonder if any of them are going to stop trying to tell me what to do long enough to see what's at the end of their own nose.</p>",
